{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC3 STATUS — a live run was executed; it satisfies the criterion as WRITTEN but does not exercise the\nfixed path. Stating both so the gap is a decision, not an accident.\n\nTHE RUN\n  command  rebar review-plan 5e75-522e-70d1-4363\n  tree     origin/main @ 144bb02251ec052d71fff029b8fce71c4d12cce0 (this fix merged)\n  verdict  PASS, signed/certified\n  counts   blocking 0, advisory_surfaced 4, dropped 1, INDETERMINATE 0\n  outcome_counts  clean 1, recovered 0, empty_outcomes 0, unrecoverable 0\n  verify_requests 10\n\nAGAINST AC3 AS WRITTEN (\"a real plan-review run emits no contract violation and findings retain\ntheir verified severity rather than degrading to INDETERMINATE\"): met. No contract violation was\nemitted, indeterminate is 0, and the four surfaced findings carry real verified severities\n(critical / minor) with populated verification blocks — not a degraded batch.\n\nWHY THAT IS STILL NOT PROOF OF THE FIX. This ticket's own census established PERFECT separation: all\n43 violations were ZERO-finding runs, and 2778 multi-finding runs produced none. A run with findings\ntherefore could not have violated even before the fix, so it cannot discriminate. empty_outcomes 0\nconfirms directly that no empty batch was synthesised on this run — the repaired branch never\nexecuted. Citing this run as AC3 evidence would be citing a test that passes on the unfixed code too.\n\nWHAT WOULD ACTUALLY DISCRIMINATE, and why it was not simply produced: a live run whose Pass-1 yields\nZERO findings. That is roughly 1 percent of historical runs (43 of 3908) and cannot be commanded —\nplan quality is the input, and every candidate ticket in this epic currently attracts findings.\nForcing one means repeated full-price review runs with no guarantee.\n\nTHE DETERMINISTIC PROOF DOES EXIST AND IS GREEN: tests/unit/test_verify_empty_batch_contract.py,\n4 passed at this tree. That is AC2 (fails before the fix) and it exercises exactly the branch a\nzero-finding live run would reach.\n\nRECOMMENDATION for the operator, not applied unilaterally: either (a) accept AC3 on the literal\nreading plus the AC2 regression test, recording that the live path is covered deterministically\nrather than in production, or (b) narrow AC3 to name the zero-finding precondition explicitly and\nkeep it open until an organic zero-finding run appears. I have NOT edited the AC, because changing an\nacceptance criterion to match the evidence I happen to have is the failure mode this ticket exists to\ncatch."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785703772231627001,"uuid":"db9a93c3-a484-4552-a374-48365ae0bc70"}